# GRID Ecosystem

Read `docs/EXITMANIA_GRID_INTEGRATION.md`, `docs/GRID_LAYER_MODEL.md`, and `.cursor/rules/product-direction.mdc` before integration or content work.

## Ownership

- **GRID (this repo):** Live engine — FSM, Alpha/Beta/Gamma, Realtime, Cockpit, layer-based content. Later: customer Studio (overwrites only), credits to activate, org data
- **Exitmania (../Developer/exitmania):** Public storefront + impulse commerce — replaces Loquiz with GRID, does NOT reimplement gameplay. Small teamevents (~€200, light custom route) stay here
- **Tabbrain:** discarded — do not build. Large groups and self-serve are GRID subscriptions, not a third brand

## Content (Layer model)

- **Layer 1:** `local_waypoints` (outdoor GPS) + `local_stations` (indoor codes) + city-scoped tasks
- **Layer 2:** `global_levels` (global mission — one content, all surfaces)
- **Layer 3:** logic rules + role assignments (bonus, Micro-Pulse)
- Surfaces: outdoor | indoor | online (GRID pulse / later 15-min); dual fallback; phases Hub → Quiz → Level → Bonus
- Per booking: `events.content_config` + `events.route_override` (GPS + station code deltas)
- Never duplicate full route JSON per event
- See `docs/GRID_LAYER_MODEL.md` for Studio priorities

## Booking API

Exitmania (and later GRID customer Studio) provision via `POST /api/v1/bookings` with `booking_reference` (idempotent), `content_pack_slug`, optional `route_override`.

## Do not

- Add checkout/Paddle to GRID
- Add CMS for master content to GRID (use migrations or future Exitmania pack pipeline)
- Build separate game runtime in Exitmania
- Use permanent WebSockets for `pulse_sessions` (REST + `pulse_player_states` only)
